'''Kaadedhdhoo Airport''' {{airport codes|KDM|VRMT}} is a [[domestic airport]] on the island of [[Kaadedhdhoo]] in [[Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll|Gaafu Dhaalu (South Huvadhu) atoll]], [[Maldives]].<ref name="Airport" /><ref name="WAD" /> The airport is located {{convert|3.7|km|NM|lk=out}} south of [[Thinadhoo (Gaafu Dhaalu Atoll)|Thinadhoo]].<ref name="Airport" /> It was opened on 10 December 1993, by [[President Maumoon Abdul Gayoom]].

==Facilities==
The airport resides at an [[elevation]] of {{convert|2|ft|m|1}} above [[mean sea level]]. It has one [[runway]] designated 16/34 with a [[bitumen|bituminous]] surface measuring {{convert|1220|x|30|m|0}}.<ref name="Airport" /><ref name="WAD" />

